CB010846_RU_resilency_uncontrolled_case_l1soc_crash
    [Documentation]
    ...  Purpose of this test case is to check if RMOD with activated feature did not reset after BBMOD autonomous reset
    ...  caused by L1 SoC crash failure.
    ...
    ...  ARGS:
    ...  :param (int or str) rmod_id: (Mandatory) : RMOD configuration id of tested radio module, e.g.: 1
    ...  :param (str) name_of_bbmod_process: name of BBMOD's process to kill and generate SoC crash failure,
    ...                                      defaults to `/usr/bin/l1_application_rt`
    ...  :param (dict) throughputs: dict with throughput and deviation values for each teste RMOD's cell identified by it's nrCellIdentity.
    ...                             Example:
    ...                               {
    ...                                   '827736065':
    ...                                        {
    ...                                             'throughput':
    ...                                                {
    ...                                                    'downlink': '100 Mbits/sec',
    ...                                                    'uplink': '15 Mbits/sec'
    ...                                                 },
    ...                                            'deviation': '90%'
    ...                                        },
    ...                                }
    ...                             Defaults to ${None} which means data transfer will not be performed in the test.
    ...  :param (str) protocol: data transfer protocol; defaults to UDP.
    ...  :param (str) udp_buffer: monitoring data buffer; defaults to 4M.
    ...  :param (bool) tput_verification_via_btslog: True - throughput verification will be performed using btslog
    ...                                              False - throuput verification will be performed using iperf; defaults to False
    ...  :param (dict) ue_network_modes: dict with UE serial numbers and desired network modes e.g. {"SN1234": "NR_only"}
    ...                                  possible UE network modes: NR_only, LTE_only, NR_LTE
    ...                                  when using more than one UE please make sure that the modes you choose are either all
    ...                                  with "_only" suffix or all "NR_LTE" as it is not yet possible to mix those.
    ...                                  mandatory for SA+NSA setups, defaults to None
    ...  :param (dict) ues_and_cells: dict with UE serial numbers and lists of configuration distnames of cells to which they
    ...                               can be attached e.g. {"SN1234": ["MRBTS-50146/NRBTS-1/NRCELL-1", "MRBTS-50146/NRBTS-1/NRCELL-3"],
    ...                                                     "SN5678": ["MRBTS-50146/NRBTS-1/NRCELL-5"]}
    ...                               defaults to ${None} which means that all UEs will be attached to all cells.
    ...                               when given, listed cells will be called in pairs with specified UEs, if there are more
    ...                               cells on the setup that were not mentioned in the list, they will be called with all UEs


    [Arguments]    ${rmod_id}
    ...            ${name_of_bbmod_process}=/usr/bin/l1_application_rt
    ...            ${throughputs}=${None}
    ...            ${protocol}=udp
    ...            ${udp_buffer}=4M
    ...            ${tput_verification_via_btslog}=${False}
    ...            ${ue_network_modes}=${None}
    ...            ${ues_and_cells}=${None}

    ${bts_type}                                             hwpta_testline.get_type_of_setup
    ${connection}                                           connections.get_default_admin_connection_alias
    ...                                                     bts_type=${bts_type}

    ${impacted_bbmod_id}                                    Get BBMOD ID Connected to RMOD by Configuration Link
    ...                                                     rmod_id=${rmod_id}
    ...                                                     connection=${connection}
    ${list_with_impacted_bbmod_id}                          Create list
    ...                                                     ${impacted_bbmod_id}

    ${rmod_startup_before_bbmod_reset}                      Get DateTime of Last RMOD Startup
    ...                                                     rmod_id=${rmod_id}
    ...                                                     connection=${connection}

    ${impacted_rmod_ids}                                    Get impacted RMODs For Impacted BBMOD
    ...                                                     impacted_bbmod_id=${impacted_bbmod_id}
    ...                                                     connection=${connection}

    ${all_cells_of_rmod}                                    admin_info_model.get_configuration_distnames_of_all_cells_for_rmod
    ...                                                     rmod_id=${rmod_id}
    ...                                                     connection=${connection}

    Kill Process on BBMOD and Wait for BBMOD Autonomous Reset
    ...                                                     bbmod_id=${impacted_bbmod_id}
    ...                                                     bbmod_cpu=1
    ...                                                     process_name=${name_of_bbmod_process}
    ...                                                     connection=${connection}

    Alarms.Allow alarm                                      fault_name=SoC autonomous reset as recovery action
    ...                                                     fault_id=2087
    ...                                                     alarm_id=7101
    ...                                                     bts_type=${bts_type}
    Alarms.Allow Diagnostic Files Collected alarms
    Alarms.Allow X2 Link Alarms

    Sleep                                                   15s
    ...                                                     reason=Waiting for status update of all components...

    Verify All BBMODs Statuses and Their Resources with Impacted BBMODs and RMODs
    ...                                                     impacted_bbmod_ids=${list_with_impacted_bbmod_id}
    ...                                                     impacted_bbmods_status_variant=degraded
    ...                                                     alternative_impacted_bbmods_status_variant=failed
    ...                                                     impacted_rmods_ids=${impacted_rmod_ids}
    ...                                                     impacted_rmods_status_variant=disabled
    ...                                                     alternative_impacted_rmods_status_variant=offline
    ...                                                     impacted_cells_status_variant=failed
    ...                                                     connection=${connection}
    ...                                                     bts_type=${bts_type}

    Check Statuses after BBMOD Autonomous Reset and Wait for OnAir
    ...                                                     bts_type=${bts_type}

    Alarms.Disallow alarm                                   fault_id=2087
    ...                                                     fault_name=SoC autonomous reset as recovery action
    ...                                                     bts_type=${bts_type}

    ${rmod_startup_after_bbmod_reset}                       Get DateTime of Last RMOD Startup
    ...                                                     rmod_id=${rmod_id}
    ...                                                     connection=${connection}

    Robot Log Operation                                     Verifying if RMOD-${rmod_id} has been reset during capacity unit reset...
    Verify If RMOD Has Been Reset                           reference_startup_datetime=${rmod_startup_before_bbmod_reset}
    ...                                                     actual_startup_datetime=${rmod_startup_after_bbmod_reset}
    ...                                                     expect_rmod_reset=${False}
    Robot Log Result                                        RMOD-${rmod_id} has not been reset during capacity unit reset.

    Run keyword if                                          ${throughputs}
    ...                                                     Run keywords
    ...                                                     Robot Log Operation
    ...                                                     Checking L3 call availiability on cells commissioned on impacted RMOD-${rmod_id}
    ...                                                     AND
    ...                                                     Execute L3 call
    ...                                                     cells_distnames=${all_cells_of_rmod}
    ...                                                     throughputs=${throughputs}
    ...                                                     protocol=${protocol}
    ...                                                     udp_buffer=${udp_buffer}
    ...                                                     tput_verification_via_btslog=${tput_verification_via_btslog}
    ...                                                     ue_network_modes=${ue_network_modes}
    ...                                                     ues_and_cells=${ues_and_cells}
    ...                                                     AND
    ...                                                     Robot Log Operation
    ...                                                     L3 call is available on impacted RMOD-${rmod_id}.

    [Teardown]                                              RU Resilency BBMOD L1 Soc Crash Teardown
    ...                                                     bts_type=${bts_type}

